+## Selected differences on the first page
 
-All four PDFs have different hashes. For the first page, the three difference boxes end at or above zero-indexed row **42** of **795**. Matching pixels in the 09:20 block and matching annotations show the dependence of the four versions in that region. Archive copy counts cannot add independent reports of the notification. All nine corresponding rendered pages differed in each sibling-to-AAL-77 comparison. The location and meaning of those differences were checked for page 1 only. I visually inspected all four first pages, checked the UAL 175 p. 9 header and footer across the render and text layer, and inspected the relevant AWA-659 headers, footers and page 4. The review did not establish a chronology of the scans. [Exact body, render and locator pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+The three mirrored copies preserve separate 0920 rows for the NMCC notification and the primary-net request. In the Team 8 and New York copies, handwriting by those rows reads `by primary net`. In the Team 7 image, different handwriting in that area appears to read `Continuous open line`. The crossed-out wording, authorship and annotation dates remain open. The printed request, the recorded notification and the handwriting are separate observations. A native bridge log or recording would test when participants joined and what they received. [Source and region locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
 
-Keep the edit approval and source for the public 09:20 wording open alongside the original event log and the NMCC connection record. The fax continuation also leaves the printed page 13 and full delivery chain open. The corrected May 2003 Commission answer and proof of delivery, signed administrative decision and recommendation follow-up remain outstanding. [Exact text comparison](TEXT-CHANGES.diff)
+The New York copy shows handwritten `8:56.` beside the printed `1256Z` in the separate **0924** radar-loss report row. The printed value is visible on the image and absent from the embedded extraction of that row. The Team 8 extraction retains `1256Z`. The handwritten number has no visible time zone in the inspected region. The source for the annotation, the time of actual radar loss and the time the report reached a recipient remain separate questions. These copies reproduce the same underlying report and their marks supply version evidence. [Source and region locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+The three new AWA-659 images show the same printed p. 12 footer in the continuation. The UAL 93 embedded footer reads `Pagel2of 13`. The AAL 11 and UAL 175 extractions omit that footer. These text layers are search aids. The image readings and exact extracted observations are retained separately. [UAL 93](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597172) · [AAL 11](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597945) · [UAL 175](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7598489)
+
+## Verification and remaining records
+
+The check verified three official catalog and PDF pairs, three individually retrieved ZIP members against their byte-range receipts and CRCs, and the physical page counts. Visual scope covered the selected first-page rows, report boundaries and the complete Team 7 p. 13. The mirror’s member paths and the official finding-aid folder descriptions have different evidentiary roles. Whole-document content comparisons and the lineage or ordering of marginal annotations remain open. [Source pins and verification scope](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+The exact September 14 fax cover, page manifest and recipient intake would establish which copy and pages were sent and received. The corrected May 2003 answer and acknowledgment, signed administrative decision, and OIG recommendation disposition remain open. This finding closes the bounded search for one copy of printed p. 13. [Open FAA records](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/README.md) · [Comparison with prior report](TEXT-CHANGES.diff)
